### Sievert Integral

\[\int_{0}^{\theta}e^{-z\,\sec\,\theta}d\phi\]

**Relation to the Error Function**

\[\int_{0}^{\theta}e^{-z\,\sec\,\theta}d\phi\sim\sqrt{\frac{\pi}{2z}}\,e^{-z}\, \operatorname{erf}\left(\sqrt{\frac{x}{2}}\,\theta\right)\quad\left(x\to\infty\right)\]

(For erf, see chapter 7.)

**Representation in Terms of Exponential Integrals**

\[\int_{0}^{\theta}e^{-z\,\sec\,\theta}d\phi= \int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}}e^{-z\,\sec\,\theta}d\phi\] \[-\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\alpha_{k}(\cos\,\theta)^{2k+1}E_{2+2}\left( \frac{x}{\cos\,\theta}\right)\] \[\left(x\geq 0,0<\theta<\frac{\pi}{2}\right)\] \[\alpha_{0}= 1,\alpha_{k}= \frac{1\cdot 3\cdot 5\ldots(2k-1)}{2\cdot 4\cdot 6\ldots(2k)}\]

(For \(E_{2k+2}(x)\), see chapter 5.)

Relation to the Integral of the Bessel Function \(K_{\theta}(x)\)

\[\int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}}e^{-z\,\sec\,\theta}d\phi= \operatorname{Ki}_{1}(x)= \int_{x}^{\infty}K_{0}(t)dt\text{ where }\] \[x|e^{z}\operatorname{Ki}_{1}(x)\sim \left(\frac{1}{2}x\right)^{\beta}\left\{1-\frac{5}{8x}+\frac{129}{12 8x^{2}}\right.\] \[\left.-\frac{2655}{1024x^{3}}+\frac{301035}{32768x^{4}}\ldots\right\}\] (For Ki,(x), see chapter 11.)